人自然忽略他面容的精致无双。这样的一张脸，一般小孩看到都会被吓坏吧。灵鸠的第一感觉是惊艳，紧接着就是涌入心间的揪心，为这样澄澈温柔的他有这样的厄运感到不值不满。少年也看着她，眼神始终没有任何的压迫力，打量或者怀疑，平和得宛若一汪温泉水。足足五秒后，少年又发出灿烂的笑声。灵鸠看去，他双眼都笑成了月牙儿，呦！还在缩小，都成了一条弯弧。他的嘴唇笑开，露出洁白的牙齿，灿烂单纯，毫不做作，毫无含蓄，最是纯粹简单不过了。“噗嗤……噗，哈，哈哈哈。”灵鸠看着看着，不自觉跟着笑，越笑越大最后完全没有了拘谨仪态。两个人，一大一小坐在草地上，跟傻子似的看着对方笑。一会儿，少年眯着眼睛，问道：“你笑什么？”灵鸠嘴巴咧着，傻傻道：“看你笑，我就想笑。”“笑得真傻。”少年道。灵鸠不生气，翻了个白眼，道：“你更傻！”两人又大眼瞪小眼，最后灵鸠表情一僵，小小的手捂住自己的半边脸。“怎么了？”少年笑容一消，紧张的问道。灵鸠没有说话。少年神情眼神的紧张更浓，连身上的气质也渐渐弥漫一股悲戚感觉。灵鸠对负面气息向来很敏感，一发觉就朝少年看去，对上他深沉的眼神顿觉揪心，撇开眼睛低低说道：“只是笑抽了。”“嗯？”“笑抽了。”“……”“笑得皮肤抽经了，够明白了吧！”“噗。”虽然被笑话了，让灵鸠倍感忧伤，不过感觉弥漫少年周围的孤寂悲戚气息散去，她又觉得挺值得。“你叫什么名字？”笑声渐止的少年问道。“灵鸠。”这回灵鸠没有犹豫告知，昂头和少年对视在一起，一秒后又补充一句，“百里灵鸠。”“灵鸠，灵鸠……”少年低低念着，似乎要细致品味其中，将之深刻脑海。灵鸠心跳跟着少年的呢喃一顿再顿。久远的记忆里，只有还没有抛弃她之前的父母叫她名字时，让她感受到温柔，被包容的甜蜜。她以为再也不会有这样感觉，可少年叫她的名字时，让她感觉到一种被珍视珍惜的温暖。“别叫了。”灵鸠悄然的握紧了手。少年没有听清楚她的声音，自顾自的笑道：“百里灵鸠，你一定是上天送给我最好的生辰礼物。”“生辰，礼物？”灵鸠一怔。日光下，少年的笑容如许，璀璨却不刺目，“七日前，我十三岁的生辰。”“……生日快乐。”千言万语凝聚心口，最终只化作了这一声最简朴的祝福。“嗯。”少年满足的笑容宛若得到了一切，笑着道：“鸠儿，你真好。”“……”灵鸠觉得自己被萌杀了，表情当即僵硬呆木。这一刻灵鸠无比的庆幸自己生在一个小孩的身体里，要不然她一个成年人竟然被一个少年掌控了心情，还弄得完全不知所措，实在太丢脸了有木有！“你高兴就好了。”只是灵鸠这一刻唯一的想法。“我叫宋雪衣……”少年刚道。“哈？！”灵鸠身体比思想更快的反应。“嗯？”她反应大得让少年一怔，不由停止了之前的话。“宋雪衣，宋家的那位大少爷？”灵鸠瞪眼，事情不会这么巧吧？宋雪衣轻轻点头。灵鸠一时看着他没有说话，脑子一片的混乱。宋雪衣，她接下来在宋家生存的衣食父母，用孙谷兰的话来说就是她想活得好，就必须讨得宋雪衣的喜爱。呃……按情况来看，她算是得到宋雪衣喜爱了吧，这样也免了之前她一直考虑的计划。宋雪衣，宋雪衣，御海镇人人都知道的病秧子……灵鸠在思考的期间，宋雪衣一直没有说话，安静看着她，眼神渐渐又恢复了平日的静谧。鸠儿，知道了我的身份，是否连你也会厌弃了我？宋雪衣心思一瞬起伏，却没有任何愤怒恼恨的情绪。“那就是这样吧。”眼前的女孩终于开口，说出来的话依旧莫名其妙，让人一时猜不透她脑袋里到底是怎么想的。“这样？”宋雪衣顺着她的问。他依旧有着一丝奢望，哪怕厌弃，也不要立即排斥好吗。灵鸠认真看着他，咬字清晰道：“宋雪衣，接下来的日子，我会负责疗养好你的身子，保护你，照顾你！”“……”为什么不回答？灵鸠疑惑，下一刻又悟了。她现在个小娃身子，说这个话估计没什么可信度。“不管你信不信，反正我信就行了。”灵鸠撇开眼，心想这孩子怎么了，眼神忽然那么煽情干嘛，太温柔她受不了好吗！再看下去她估计又得说不出心里话了！这一次，灵鸠没有等多久就听到了宋雪衣的回应，他问：“我需要付出什么？”灵鸠一怔，想了想，道：“笑吧，多笑一点，你笑起来真好看。”视线放在别处的灵鸠没有看见，宋雪衣的眼神紧紧的落在她的身上，那眼神浓郁得让人动容。“……好。”他微微垂眸。灵鸠感觉身上的视线淡去，这才转头看向他，露出一个真诚的笑容，“宋雪衣，你值得最好的。”像你这样的人，不该承受这些苦难。", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/qingbenheimengzhiyaofeilaixi/4.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 004 The beautiful young Lingjiu picked up a piece of crystal cake, glanced at the young man quietly, and then lowered his head. \"Pfft - like a squirrel.\" The young man laughed again, and Qingyue's laughter easily infected others. Lingjiu glared at him and swallowed quietly. She was very quiet when she was eating, as quietly as if she was afraid of disturbing something, making it difficult for others to notice. But once you notice her, you will be unconsciously attracted to the tranquility. The young man sat next to him, clasping his chin with one hand and watching. It was obvious that he was wearing a mask on his face, but Lingjiu glanced at him occasionally, but felt that the expression behind his mask must be smiling, and it was still the kind of gentle and heart-wrenching smile. \"Don't you want to eat?\" Lingjiu was so shocked that the hairs on her skin stood up. She finally couldn't bear it and spoke, but she regretted it as soon as she spoke. Let me go, Lingjiu, have you traveled through time and become a child, and your mind has become stupid? One look at him showed that he had an extraordinary status and had never eaten anything good. Besides, he was wearing a mask. It was obvious that he didn’t want others to see his face! She pretended to be a child's ignorance, but the truth was that she didn't realize that her expression had completely turned into an embarrassment, pretending to be innocent, \"Ah, my eldest brother must have eaten a lot of delicious food, he must not want to eat it... right? Uh!\" In front of him, the young man had already stretched out his hand that looked like white snow and jade, lifted up the strange mask on his face, and revealed his face bit by bit. The first thing that caught the eye was the young man's slender chin, then the lavender lips that were slightly raised with a pure smile of pleasure, and then the slightly delicate and straight nose, and finally a pair of eyebrows and eyes that were like painted with splashed ink. The thick eyelashes drooped, casting a shadow that made his pupils deeper and hazy. He looked at her, peaceful and tranquil. This is a young man who can be called beautiful. His facial features are so exquisite that even women would feel ashamed in front of him. It's a pity that his pale face and cheeks are covered with light blue meridians, as if his cheeks are about to crack. At first glance, he reveals a bit of terror, and then people naturally ignore the exquisiteness of his face. With a face like this, most children would be frightened when they see it. Lingjiu's first feeling was one of surprise, and then came the heart-wrenching feeling that poured into his heart. He felt unworthy of such a misfortune for such a clear and gentle man. The young man also looked at her, his eyes never showing any pressure, scrutinizing or doubting, as calm as a pool of hot spring water. Five full seconds later, the boy burst into brilliant laughter again. Lingjiu looked at him and saw that his eyes were smiling like crescent moons, yo! Still shrinking, it has become a curved arc. His lips parted in a smile, revealing his white teeth, bright and simple, without any pretense or subtlety, nothing could be more pure and simple. \"Pfft... Pfft, ha, hahaha.\" Lingjiu looked at it and laughed unconsciously. The smile got bigger and bigger, and finally he lost all restraint. Two people, one big and one small, were sitting on the grass, looking at each other and laughing like fools. After a while, the young man squinted his eyes and asked, \"Why are you laughing?\" Lingjiu grinned and said stupidly, \"Seeing you smile makes me want to laugh.\" \"You are so silly,\" the young man said. Lingjiu was not angry, but rolled his eyes and said, \"You are even more stupid!\" The two stared at each other again, and finally Lingjiu's expression froze and he covered half of his face with his small hands. \"What's wrong?\" The boy's smile faded and he asked nervously. Lingjiu said nothing. The young man's expression and eyes became more nervous, and even his body's temperament gradually became filled with a sense of sadness. Lingjiu has always been very sensitive to negative auras. As soon as he noticed it, he looked towards the young man and felt heartbroken when he saw his deep eyes. He turned away his eyes and said in a low voice: \"I just laughed so hard.\" \"Huh?\" \"I laughed so hard.\" \"... \"...\" \"My skin is throbbing with laughter, that's enough!\" \"Pfft.\" Although Lingjiu felt sad after being laughed at, she felt that it was worth it when the loneliness and sadness surrounding the young man disappeared. \"What's your name?\" asked the boy whose laughter gradually stopped. \"Lingjiu.\" This time Lingjiu told him without hesitation. He raised his head and looked at the young man, and added a second later, \"Lingjiu Baili.\" \"Lingjiu, Lingjiu...\" the young man muttered in a low voice, as if he wanted to savor it carefully and ingrain it in his mind. Lingjiu's heart beat again and again following the young man's murmur. In her long-lasting memory, only when her parents called her name before abandoning her, she felt the sweetness of tenderness and tolerance. She thought she would never feel like this again, but when the boy called her name, she felt the warmth of being cherished. \"Stop screaming.\" Lingjiu quietly clenched his hand. The young man did not hear her voice clearly and smiled to himself: \"Baili Lingjiu, you must be the best birthday gift God has given me.\" \"Birthday, gift?\" Lingjiu was startled. Under the sunlight, the young man's smile was like this, bright but not dazzling, \"Seven days ago, it was my thirteenth birthday.\" \"...Happy birthday.\" Thousands of words gathered in my heart, and finally turned into this simple blessing. \"Yes.\" The young man's satisfied smile seemed to have gained everything, and he said with a smile: \"Jiu'er, you are so kind.\" \"...\" Lingjiu felt that he was killed by cuteness, and his expression immediately became stiff and dull. At this moment, Lingjiu was extremely grateful that she was born in the body of a child. Otherwise, it would be so embarrassing for her as an adult to have her mood controlled by a teenager and be completely at a loss! \"As long as you're happy.\" was Lingjiu's only thought at this moment. \"My name is Song Xueyi...\" the young man just said. \"Huh?!\" Lingjiu's body reacted faster than his mind. \"Huh?\" Her reaction was so loud that the young man was startled and couldn't help but stop what he was saying. \"Song Xueyi, the eldest young master of the Song family?\" Lingjiu glared, it couldn't be such a coincidence, could it? Song Xueyi nodded lightly. Lingjiu looked at him without speaking for a moment, his mind in confusion. Song Xueyi, her next living parent in the Song family, in Sun Gulan’s words,", "title_en": "Chapter 4"}